runtime/csrc/tp/peer_oneshot_allreduce.cu
runtime/include/sparkinfer/tp/peer_oneshot_allreduce.h
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Implements the same one-shot all-reduce algorithm as vLLM's
`cross_device_reduce_1stage` / `cross_device_reduce_2stage`, and uses the barrier
above. Original code, but the algorithm and the barrier are vLLM-derived, so the
same attribution applies.

runtime/csrc/tp/multimem_allreduce.cu
runtime/include/sparkinfer/tp/multimem_allreduce.h
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Original code. Uses the CUDA driver multicast VMM API (cuMulticast*) and
`multimem.*` PTX directly; it shares only the barrier from tp_allreduce.cuh.

kernels/include/sparkinfer/kernels/iq2xs_tables.h
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The IQ2_XS lattice and sign tables (iq2xs_grid[512], ksigns_iq2xs[128],
kmask_iq2xs[8]) are extracted verbatim from ggml/src/ggml-common.h.

    Copyright (c) 2023-2024 The ggml authors
    Licensed under the MIT License

Extracted mechanically rather than transcribed: a single wrong constant in the
512-entry lattice corrupts only the codepoints that use it, which no shape or size
check can detect. MIT-to-MIT, so no additional obligation beyond this attribution.

